     "\r<br>&gt; On May 14, 2015, at 5:36 AM, Bruno Nicenboim &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">bruno.n...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; ok, thanks!\r<br>&gt; And while we are at this. It&#39;s impossible to use &quot;get_inits&quot; when a model fails, it will be nice to be able to extract the initial values. I don&#39;t know if this is addressed in the new version or if I could add it as a feature request (in github?)\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "It&#39;d be great if you could add it as a feature request in stan-dev/rstan.  \r<br>\r<br>I&#39;m not sure what should happen, though --- I don&#39;t think we\r<br>want to return a broken fit object when something fails.\r<br>\r<br>Right now, if you have the seed, you can use diagnostic mode,\r<br>which produces parameter values and derivatives on the unconstrained\r<br>scale, which could then be converted.  So it probably wouldn&#39;t be\r<br>hard to be able to get the init values.\r<br>\r<br>Alternatively, we might write then to an output file if that&#39;s\r<br>specified.\r<br>\r<br>- Bob"
